-- title:
--   P-primary q^m-torsion as I^m-torsion, I=(q)+Pᶜ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes. The group $J =$ `JZero p` is the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$p$ modular function field base changed to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, regarded as a module over the free Hecke algebra $\mathbb T =$ `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb Z[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ by the structure `heckeModuleBar p`: if the operators `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ` commute pairwise, the variable $X_\ell$ acts as `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ`, and otherwise all variables act by zero. Let $\mathfrak P =$ `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q` be the preimage of $(q) \subseteq \mathbb Z$ under the $\mathbb Z$-algebra map $\mathbb T \to \mathbb Z$ evaluating the variables at the Eisenstein system of level $p$. The assertion is that there is an integer $c > 0$, independent of $m$, such that for every $m \in \mathbb N$ the subgroup `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q m`, defined as the intersection of the kernel of multiplication by $q^m$ on $J$ with the supremum over $k$ of the submodules annihilated by $\mathfrak P^k$, coincides with the subgroup of elements annihilated by every element of $\left((q) + \mathfrak P^{c}\right)^m$, where $(q)$ is the ideal of $\mathbb T$ generated by the constant $q$.
--
--   This is the elementary commutative-algebra step underlying Mazur's description of the $\mathfrak P$-primary part of the $q$-power torsion of $J_0(p)$: it replaces the two-condition description of the primary torsion (killed by $q^m$ and by some power of the Eisenstein maximal ideal) by annihilation under the $m$-th power of a single fixed ideal $I = (q) + \mathfrak P^c$, so that the filtration by $m$ becomes the $I$-adic one. It is used in the analysis of the torsion sheaf on the Néron model, in the lemmas [`ModularCurve.jZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_alpha_le_filtAlpha_v5`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_alpha_le_filtAlpha_v5), [`ModularCurve.jZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_growth_two_v5`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_growth_two_v5) and [`ModularCurve.jZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_inv_linearGrowth_v5`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_inv_linearGrowth_v5).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar_eq_torsionBySet_span_sup_pow.lean

